<title>INDIA: Flash strike disrupts Indian domestic flights.</title>
<headline>Flash strike disrupts Indian domestic flights.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A nationwide flash strike by air traffic controllers disrupted domestic flights, an official of the Airports Authority of India said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said the flash strike began before noon.</p>
<p>International flights have been largely unaffected so far only because most international flights take off at night, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike is continuing. Flights have been disrupted badly,&quot; said a spokesman for state-run Indian Airlines.</p>
<p>Air traffic controllers were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>The Press Trust of India news agency said the strike was to protest against the suspension of an air traffic controller in New Delhi airport.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
